# CODEOWNERS: who must approve changes before they reach main (and therefore production).
#
# Release owners: Ammar (ammarusmani729) and Arham (arhamnasirkhan).
# With branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners", EVERY pull request needs an
# approving review from one of them (never from the PR's own author). Because an approved PR
# is auto-merged and deployed, this approval is the production release decision.
#
# Other team members review, comment and test on the preview link as usual; their approvals
# are visible but do not, on their own, allow a merge.
# Team convention on top: security-sensitive PRs (auth, access rules, migrations, scripts,
# .github/) need a second approval from another team member as well.
#
# Owners must be organization members with write access.
# Only one rule on purpose: more specific rules would replace this one for their paths
# (the last matching pattern wins).

